{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/914983-geist-1-1-errata","id":914983,"title":"Geist 1.1 Errata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-15T12:26:00-07:00","id":914983,"title":"Geist 1.1 Errata","content":"So I recently discovered that one of my favorite games, Geist, has finally gotten some errata to help balance it out a bit and smooth over all the mistakes and rough edges. However I found out that apparently White Wolf never bothered to just make it into a normal Errata document the way that companies like Wizards do, and instead updated their pdf instead and offered it to those who could prove that they had purchased the first book. Well I have a physical copy of Geist the Sin Eaters, but the offer from White Wolf to send in a picture of yourself holding the book in order to get the updated pdf is obviously long over with since they don't even own WOD anymore. So my question is this. Is there any way to get just the Errata that I don't know about? Like did anyone ever finally put together a document on their own or am I going to have to spend another 20 bucks to get the pdf from drivethrurpg? I know 20 bucks doesn't seem like that much to pay but I am extremely short on funds right now (broke), I don't really feel that it's right to make a customer pay for simple errata, however I am currently playing in a 6 man campaign that could really do with some errata. So are there any other options to get the content I need or am I forced to have to rebuy the book again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11980-emparawr","name":"Emparawr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11980_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"